add(40,
'A request needs a resource that must be released afterward. A yielding dependency supplies the resource while keeping acquisition and release in one declared boundary.',
'Acquire before yield and yield the resource to the operation. Put release in a finally block surrounding yield so cleanup covers successful use and exceptional exit. Trace two scopes: default request scope ends after the response is sent, while scope="function" ends after the handler finishes but before sending the response. Label handler completion and response sending separately on the timeline. If the dependency catches an exception it has not intentionally handled, re-raise it rather than hiding it from FastAPI. Resource cleanup and failure visibility must both remain clear. This lets you reason about when the supplied resource stops being owned by the dependency without treating yield as a generic promise of one cleanup time for all declarations.',
'A yielding dependency does not always end at handler completion. Default request scope and explicit function scope end at different points.', 'HIGH:whiteboard_drawing')
add(41,
'An order failure logged only as "failed" tells the next developer very little. Structured event fields make the outcome interpretable without relying on unexplained free text.',
'For a synthetic failure, record consistently named fields for timestamp, code location, event type, severity, result status and reason. Pass the event fields using logger.error(message, extra=event_fields), then ensure the configured formatter or collector preserves them. Attaching fields to a LogRecord is only part of the path; inspect the emitted record as well. Use custom names that do not collide with reserved LogRecord attributes.',
'An extra dictionary does not by itself establish that output preserves those fields. Check the formatter or collection pipeline.', 'MEDIUM:screen_demo')
add(42,
'A service accepts destination-related input for an outbound lookup. If that input can select any URL, the service may be directed outside its intended public-service boundary.',
'When providers are known, map the request to an allowed destination instead of accepting an arbitrary URL. For public-only access, reject private, loopback, link-local and other non-public addresses, including IPv6 equivalents. Follow the connection beyond the first hostname check: validate the resolved address actually used, because an earlier hostname check alone leaves a DNS rebinding gap. Then trace a redirect from an initially permitted destination. Either disable automatic redirects or apply the same checks to each target. Work through requested destination, connected address and redirect target separately. A policy covering only the first stage is not the same boundary as one covering where the connection actually goes.',
'A permitted-looking hostname alone is insufficient. The connected address and redirect targets must respect the destination policy too.', 'HIGH:whiteboard_drawing')
add(43,
'An upload endpoint accepts an attachment and form metadata. Multipart input is untrusted body data, so declaring UploadFile does not establish all resource limits.',
'Bind metadata with Form and the attachment with File and UploadFile, with python-multipart installed. UploadFile uses a spooled file and supports asynchronous resource methods. Configure RequestBodyLimitMiddleware with finite max_body_size for the supplied total body budget; incoming bytes include multipart overhead, and excess returns 413. Separately bound file count, field count and non-file field size through request.form options. Compare many small fields with an oversized total body: parser controls and total body limits answer different questions. Reject disallowed content types and validate fields before processing, then close the file when finished. Treat the body budget as actual bytes received, not an assumption based on how the caller describes the attachment.',
'A spooled upload is not an unlimited-input policy. Multipart parser limits also do not replace a total actual-body-byte limit.', 'HIGH:screen_demo')
add(44,
'A browser client needs permission to call an API across origins. Configure for that client without confusing browser access with endpoint access control.',
'For a hypothetical client at https://shop.example, list that origin and the required methods and headers in CORSMiddleware configuration. Defaults are restrictive: methods default to GET and credentials to false. If credentialed access is needed, set allow_credentials=True and explicitly list origins, methods and headers rather than wildcards. Compare each policy dimension with the intended browser call. A matching origin alone does not explain whether the method and headers are allowed. After this browser-access policy is established, the API still needs endpoint access checks. Draw that as a separate boundary so middleware is not presented as a replacement for authentication or authorization.',
'CORS grants browser response access, not caller authority. Credentialed configuration requires explicit origins, methods and headers.')
add(45,
'Two providers in one request may need the same dependency result. FastAPI normally reuses it within the request, not as application-wide storage.',
'Label the provider result for request A as value A. Have two dependants declare the same provider and verify reuse within A. Then send request B and inspect it independently rather than assuming value A is service-wide. If one declaration needs fresh execution, use Depends(provider, use_cache=False) there. Trace resolution with and without that setting to identify where another execution is required. The default cache reduces repeated dependency execution within a request; its boundary is that request, not all clients or worker processes. This matters when interpreting a provider returning a request-specific value.',
'Dependency caching is normally request-local. It is not a substitute for application-wide storage.', 'HIGH:whiteboard_drawing')
add(46,
'Calling a handler directly can miss routing or dependency problems. An endpoint integration test exercises the application\'s HTTP boundary.',
'Create TestClient(app), send a request to the declared order path, and assert response.status_code and response.json() in a test_ function run by pytest. The request goes through route and dependency resolution, unlike a direct handler call. If the case requires lifespan resources, use with TestClient(app) as client so setup and teardown execute. Separate two questions: did the endpoint produce the intended HTTP outcome, and did the test execute the required application-lifetime boundary? A body assertion alone does not establish status, while status alone does not establish projected content. Choose a concrete order response and inspect both.',
'A direct function call is not an HTTP endpoint test. Execute lifespan with the TestClient context when the case needs it.', 'HIGH:live_code')
add(47,
'An order note can be required to appear while allowing null as its value. Presence and nullability should not collapse into one "optional" case.',
'Compare note: str | None without a default with note: str | None = None. The first requires presence but admits null. The second permits omission and explicit null. Send three bodies: one omitting note, one supplying null and one supplying a concrete note. Compare each with the declaration rather than treating them as interchangeable. For a field without a default, missing presence is the issue; for a nullable type, null is a permitted value. A two-axis table labeled presence and value keeps a default from being mistaken for a type choice. This clarifies the input contract before later partial-update behavior uses presence to express intent.',
'Nullable does not automatically mean omittable. A nullable field without a default still requires presence.', 'LOW:data_table_demo')
add(48,
'Typed declarations also describe the public API contract. Generated OpenAPI connects operation entries with the input and output schemas they contribute.',
'Retrieve /openapi.json for an order operation. Find its method entry under paths and follow schema references into components. Compare the body model with the input schema and the response model with the output schema. Trace an input field and an output field through these references so you can explain which operation uses each definition. The task is understanding generated structure and its connection to declarations, not assuming documentation proves every runtime outcome. Following references bridges the operation entry and the reusable definitions it points to.',
'An operation may reference schemas in components. Do not assume every field detail appears inline.', 'HIGH:screen_demo')
add(49,
'A deployment should accept only intended request host identities. TrustedHostMiddleware checks this Host boundary independently of other metadata.',
'Configure allowed_hosts with intended domain names. An unallowed Host gets 400. Compare an exact domain with *.example.com, permitting subdomains, and ["*"], permitting any host. These are different policies. Account for www_redirect, whose default true behavior can redirect an allowed non-www host to its www counterpart. In verification, record the supplied Host and observed response rather than assuming all allowed cases look identical. Trace rejection separately from an allowed redirect. This keeps requested host identity separate from authentication or trust in forwarded proxy metadata.',
'An all-host wildcard removes the selective allowlist boundary. Allowed non-www cases may redirect under www_redirect.', 'HIGH:screen_demo')
add(50,
'A useful diagnostic record must not expose credentials or personal information. Redaction covers supplemental context as well as the main message.',
'Exercise a synthetic failure with a recognizable fake token and fake connection-string secret. Inspect the full emitted record, including extra fields. Under the supplied logging policy, remove or mask prohibited values while retaining intended event fields. Success means the diagnostic remains interpretable without prohibited synthetic strings, not merely that the main message looks safe.',
'A safe message can still have unsafe context. Inspect the emitted record, not just the message template.', 'MEDIUM:screen_demo')
add(51,
'A database session holds mutable state for current work. Concurrent requests should not become concurrent users of one shared session.',
'Build an async_sessionmaker bound to the async engine. For each request unit of work, use async with session_factory() as session to obtain and close a session. A dependency can yield it from that context, preserving normal and exceptional cleanup. Draw request A with session A and request B with session B. They may share factory setup, but mutable sessions belong to separate concurrent work units. One application-wide session borrowed by both tasks violates this boundary. Follow ownership from creation through dependency use to context exit; cleanup should not depend solely on the successful return branch.',
'A shared factory is not permission to share one AsyncSession across concurrent tasks.', 'HIGH:whiteboard_drawing')
add(52,
'A deployment terminates while an order request is active. Graceful shutdown is a bounded opportunity for work and cleanup, not indefinite waiting.',
'Configure --timeout-graceful-shutdown with the supplied maximum wait. Terminate during a controlled active request and observe whether its response completes within that limit. Inspect whether lifespan cleanup releases shared resources. Old processes stop accepting new connections and active responses and background tasks have configured time to finish; after the maximum wait Uvicorn starts terminating remaining requests.',
'Graceful does not mean unlimited time or guaranteed completion. Verify response behavior and resource cleanup against the bound.', 'HIGH:screen_demo')
add(53,
'A process can be alive while unable to serve traffic because a required backend is temporarily unavailable. Liveness and readiness express different decisions.',
'Configure separate livenessProbe and readinessProbe HTTP checks with supplied path, port, periodSeconds and failureThreshold. Trace a backend outage while the process remains alive: readiness can remove traffic eligibility without requiring restart. Failed liveness can cause restart. HTTP probes classify 200 through 399 as success, other codes as failure. Compare this with the intended probe contract; calling a body "unready" is not enough if its status still counts as successful. Draw restart and traffic eligibility separately so a dependency outage is not automatically treated as proof that restarting is intended.',
'Alive does not necessarily mean ready. HTTP probe success includes 3xx, not just 200.', 'HIGH:whiteboard_drawing')
add(54,
'Public examples should clarify an order operation\'s executable contract, not describe incompatible accepted data.',
'Use ConfigDict json_schema_extra examples or Field examples for schema samples, and Body(openapi_examples={...}) for named body examples. Before publishing an order sample, validate it with Model.model_validate(example). An incompatible sample misleads about accepted input. Add tags, summary and description to group and explain the operation without assuming they change behavior. Trace synthetic data through validation to public metadata. The validation step makes examples useful illustrations of the declared shape rather than attractive demonstrations of a different contract.',
'Descriptions do not change runtime behavior. Published examples should validate against their model.', 'MEDIUM:screen_demo')
add(55,
'An endpoint test needs a controlled provider result. Substitute at the declared dependency boundary and exercise its use through HTTP.',
'Map the original provider callable to a replacement in app.dependency_overrides. Send the request and assert behavior making the replacement observable, such as its synthetic value in the projected result. The mapping uses callables, not provider names or returned values. Restore the earlier override state afterward; reset to an empty dictionary when no prior overrides existed. Trace setup, request, assertion and restoration. Another test should not silently receive this replacement. Limit the override to the controlled input rather than substituting away behavior the test claims to verify.',
'Overrides left active can alter later tests. Restore the prior state rather than assuming automatic isolation.', 'HIGH:live_code')
add(56,
'A handler needs a header and a cookie. Explicit source markers keep these metadata inputs from becoming ordinary query parameters.',
'Declare the inputs using Header and Cookie in Annotated types. A header parameter user_agent maps to user-agent by default because underscores become hyphens, and header names are case-insensitive. Use alias or control underscore conversion when the contract requires another mapping. Give a cookie a default when omission is accepted. Trace actual request names to their declarations instead of inferring the source from a metadata-sounding name. Keep source naming and omission behavior separate so a correctly bound cookie also has the intended requiredness.',
'A metadata-looking name does not automatically bind a header. The declaration and default underscore conversion matter.')
add(57,
'Malformed order input should be rejected before normal handler logic. That differs from a validation bug in service-generated output.',
'Send a value that cannot satisfy a request field. Assert default status 422 and inspect JSON detail entries for failed input location and error type. Invalid input does not reach normal operation logic. Compare a validation failure while the service builds its own result: that indicates a server-side bug rather than this client-input rejection.',
'Not every model-validation failure is a client 422. RequestValidationError concerns invalid request data.', 'MEDIUM:live_code')
add(58,
'A metrics endpoint existing does not prove counters and durations measure intended request events. Compare maintained instrumentation against known requests.',
'Install PrometheusMiddleware with filter_unhandled_paths=True and expose the /metrics/ view from starlette_prometheus. Use bounded nonsensitive labels such as method, route template and status. Send a success, expected-error response and delayed response; compare counter changes and duration observations with those controlled requests. This middleware updates its response counter even for a raised exception, but observes processing time only when the inner application returns a response. Counts and completed-response durations therefore need not cover identical paths. Trace them before interpreting aggregates, and filter unmatched arbitrary paths rather than giving every requested path its own series.',
'A raised exception updates this middleware\'s response counter but does not produce its normal processing-time observation.', 'HIGH:screen_demo')
add(59,
'A partial update must distinguish "leave unchanged" from "set to null." Presence carries intent separately from value.',
'Stored order data has a note and quantity. An update supplying only quantity should not overwrite note with a default. Extract supplied fields with model_dump(exclude_unset=True); model_fields_set shows explicit fields. Now supply note as None. It remains in exclude_unset output because the caller supplied it and can represent an intentional null under the contract. Adding exclude_none=True removes it separately and can erase that intent. Compare omission, null and concrete values in extracted updates before applying them. The final value alone does not reveal whether a caller supplied the field.',
'exclude_unset and exclude_none answer different questions. Removing None can erase an intentional null update.', 'HIGH:data_table_demo')
